    {
      "title": "Labour wins Holborn and St Pancras byelection; Polanski ‘absolutely’ intends to remain Greens leader – UK politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/09/holborn-st-pancras-byelection-result-zack-polanski-sagal-abdi-wali-uk-labour-green-party-uk-politics-latest-news",
      "description": "<p>Sagal Abdi-Wali defeats Green party leader Zack Polanski to retain the Holborn and St Pancras seat for Labour</p><p><strong>Activists in Camden have suggested the Greens’ decision to back the anti-Zionism motion has cost them votes</strong> in the byelection.</p><p>Councillors for both Labour the Liberal Democrats told the Press Association that voters had informed them they would not be backing the Green party after it passed the motion last weekend calling Zionism racism.</p><p>It is clear now we will come a close second in this by-election. Taking the fight to Labour in one of its safest seats shows just how far the Greens have come.</p><p>Voters want us to keep Labour’s feet to the fire on affordable housing, public ownership of water and the climate crisis. Greens will be there every single day, holding Labour to account and demanding the change people voted for.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/09/holborn-st-pancras-byelection-result-zack-polanski-sagal-abdi-wali-uk-labour-green-party-uk-politics-latest-news\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-09T03:06:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Labour fends off Green party to win Holborn and St Pancras byelection",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/09/labour-wins-holborn-st-pancras-byelection-green-party",
      "description": "<p>Victory by Sagal Abdi-Wali in north London seat will be a relief for Andy Burnham in high-stakes battle for the left of British politics</p><p>Labour has won the Holborn and St Pancras byelection in a high-stakes battle for the left of British politics.</p><p>The byelection, called after the former prime minister Keir Starmer <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/01/keir-starmer-to-stand-down-as-mp\">resigned the seat</a> in September, was considered a two-horse race between the Labour candidate, Sagal Abdi-Wali, and the Green party leader, Zack Polanski. Abdi-Wali recieved 12,292 votes to Polanski’s 8,928.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/09/labour-wins-holborn-st-pancras-byelection-green-party\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-09T02:03:41"
    },
